# This repository checks its own integrity by sha256 (tools/skill-hashes.txt), so the working tree
# has to agree byte for byte on every machine. Git's line-ending normalisation would rewrite every
# LF on a Windows checkout, change the bytes, and make check_links.py report that the read-only
# skills had been edited — on a clone where nobody touched them.
#
# So: LF in the working tree everywhere, and no conversion at all for the files whose bytes are the
# guarantee.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The skills are copied byte-identical and verified by hash. Never normalise, never diff.
.claude/skills/** -text -diff

# Binary assets: the voice prompt WAVs are immutable conditioning identities.
*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.mp4 binary
